§ `Rounding and the Order's own figures -- findings F-01 and F-02`

-- The Order says "increased by 3.8 per cent" and never says how to round. Its own figures show what it did where it
-- states both ends. To the nearest penny (half up), 135.50 increased by 3.8 per cent is 140.65, which is the figure
-- art 4(2)(a) substitutes; 17.83 pence increased by 3.8 per cent is 18.50754, 18.51 to the nearest hundredth,
-- which is what art 11(1) says.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest hundredth` x MEANS FLOOR (x TIMES 100 PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 100

#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest hundredth` (135.50 TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)) EQUALS 140.65
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest hundredth` (`art 4(2)(a): section 44(4) sum replaced in paragraph (a)`'s `the sum before the Order` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)) EQUALS `art 4(2)(a): section 44(4) sum replaced in paragraph (a)`'s `the sum after the Order`
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest hundredth` (17.83 TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)) EQUALS 18.51
-- F-02: the Order's other substituted sums are NOT all 3.8 per cent. 176.45 increased by 3.8 per cent is 183.16
-- to the penny (183.1551 before rounding); art 4(2)(b) substitutes 184.90. 230.25 increased by 3.8 per cent is 239.00 to the
-- penny (238.9995 before rounding); art 6(1) substitutes 241.30.
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest hundredth` (176.45 TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)) EQUALS 183.16
#ASSERT NOT (`rounded to the nearest hundredth` (176.45 TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)) EQUALS 184.90)
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest hundredth` (230.25 TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)) EQUALS 239.00
#ASSERT NOT (`rounded to the nearest hundredth` (230.25 TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)) EQUALS 241.30)

§ `Article 7 -- dates on which the changes take effect (src:99-124)`

#ASSERT `art 7(2): the date on which the changes take effect for Category A, B, C and D retirement pension and graduated retirement benefit, with increases for dependants` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 6
#ASSERT `art 7(3): the date on which the increases in the sums mentioned in article 5 take effect` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 6
#ASSERT `art 7(4)(a): the date on which the increase in the rate of attendance allowance takes effect` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 6
#ASSERT `art 7(4)(b): the date on which the increase in the rate of carer's allowance takes effect, except where it is paid on a Wednesday` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 6
#ASSERT `art 7(5)(a)(i): the date on which the increase in the rate of carer's allowance takes effect where it is paid on a Wednesday` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 8
#ASSERT `art 7(5): the date on which the increases for disablement benefit, the maximum disablement gratuity, widow's and widower's industrial death benefit, the maximum aggregate for successive accidents, and disablement benefit and pension for dependants take effect` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 8
#ASSERT `art 7(6): the date on which the increase in a Category A or B retirement pension by reference to invalidity allowance or age addition takes effect` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 6
#ASSERT `art 7(7): the date on which the changes in the rate of incapacity benefit and severe disablement allowance, with increases for dependants, take effect` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 9
#ASSERT `art 7(8): the date on which the increases in the retirement allowance sums take effect` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 8
#ASSERT `art 7(10): the date on which the increases in the sums for state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act take effect` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 6
#ASSERT `art 7(11): the date on which the increase in the maximum additional pension takes effect` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 6

-- carer's allowance: paid on a Wednesday, 8th April; otherwise 6th April
#ASSERT `art 7(4)(b), (5)(a)(i): the date on which the increase in the rate of carer's allowance takes effect` TRUE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 8
#ASSERT `art 7(4)(b), (5)(a)(i): the date on which the increase in the rate of carer's allowance takes effect` FALSE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 6

-- (9): arguments are "regulation 7(b) applies" and the first day of the first benefit week; the threshold is 6th April,
-- or 1st April where regulation 7(b) applies
#ASSERT `art 7(9): the date on which the increase in the article 25(b) sum takes effect for the beneficiary` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 6) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `art 7(9): the date on which the increase in the article 25(b) sum takes effect for the beneficiary` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `art 7(9): the date on which the increase in the article 25(b) sum takes effect for the beneficiary` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `art 7(9): the date on which the increase in the article 25(b) sum takes effect for the beneficiary` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT `art 7(9): the date on which the increase in the article 25(b) sum takes effect for the beneficiary` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `art 7(9): the date on which the increase in the article 25(b) sum takes effect for the beneficiary` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 5) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 5)

-- (1): the date for each kind of change (arguments: which change; paid on a Wednesday; regulation 7(b) applies; the first
-- day of the first benefit week)
GIVEN c IS A `a change that art 7 dates`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`an ordinary case: the date for the change` c MEANS
    `art 7: the date on which the change takes effect` c FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 13)

#ASSERT `an ordinary case: the date for the change` `the change in the sums for Category A, B, C and D retirement pension and graduated retirement benefit, with increases for dependants` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `an ordinary case: the date for the change` `the change in the sums mentioned in article 5` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `an ordinary case: the date for the change` `the change in the rate of attendance allowance` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `an ordinary case: the date for the change` `the change in the rate of carer's allowance` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `an ordinary case: the date for the change` `the change in the rate of disablement benefit, the maximum disablement gratuity, widow's and widower's industrial death benefit, the maximum aggregate for successive accidents, and disablement benefit and pension for dependants` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 8)
#ASSERT `an ordinary case: the date for the change` `the increase in a Category A or B retirement pension by reference to invalidity allowance or age addition to long-term incapacity benefit` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `an ordinary case: the date for the change` `the change in the rate of incapacity benefit and severe disablement allowance, with increases for dependants` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 9)
#ASSERT `an ordinary case: the date for the change` `the increase in the retirement allowance sums` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 8)
#ASSERT `an ordinary case: the date for the change` `the increase in the article 25(b) sum, so far as it is relevant to the adult dependant earnings test` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 13)
#ASSERT `an ordinary case: the date for the change` `the increase in the sums for state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `an ordinary case: the date for the change` `the increase in the maximum additional pension` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 6)
-- carer's allowance paid on a Wednesday, through the dispatcher
#ASSERT `art 7: the date on which the change takes effect` `the change in the rate of carer's allowance` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 13) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 8)
-- the earnings-limit sum with regulation 7(b): a first benefit week starting 1st April qualifies
#ASSERT `art 7: the date on which the change takes effect` `the increase in the article 25(b) sum, so far as it is relevant to the adult dependant earnings test` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT `art 7: the date on which the change takes effect` `the increase in the article 25(b) sum, so far as it is relevant to the adult dependant earnings test` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS NOTHING
